    issue('registered-source',[1,16],'Registered arXiv2409.08863v1, stamped13September2024,39pages. Main text ends after acknowledgments/funding on16. Supplementary availability listings and references occupy17–18; appendix bodies start19 and are excluded. Exactly three main-text Theorems3.1–3.3; Corollary3.1 is not inventoried.')
    issue('change-index-and-gap',[3,6,8,9],'Tau denotes the first changed observation, so pre-change means stop at tau-1 and the final argmin sums through j-1. d is a positive lower bound for all post-change gaps, not necessarily the attained minimum. d_star averages the signal over sliding blocks; d_hat estimates that averaged quantity. Preserve the strict d>K*d_star inequality with K>rho; feasibility with d_star>=d implies K<1 rather than an arbitrary large constant.')
    issue('true-block-index-boundary',[5,8],'The source defines eta=floor(tau/k) and also calls it the last fully pre-change block, writing eta*k+1<=tau<=(eta+1)*k. At tau exactly divisible byk, that interval is inconsistent and the eta-th block includes the first changed observation. Retain the literal floor definition and the contradictory prose; do not silently substitute floor((tau-1)/k).')
    issue('generic-versus-specific-variance',[4,5,7,8,9],'Definitions(5) and(9) permit any consistent long-run-variance estimator; estimator(8) is a suggested canonical choice. Theorem3.2 supplies a rate for(8) under its own stronger moment/block/gap conditions. These do not become mandatory premises ofTheorem3.1, and Theorem3.3 does not require that its user-chosen variance estimate be(8). The mean muhat0 from(8) is still a required preliminary mean for(9).')
    issue('overlapping-window-normalization',[4,5],'R_(s/k) extends nonoverlapping R_j to sliding windows even for noninteger s/k. The variance estimate uses k/(ellhat-k+1), all endpoints s=k..ellhat and centering by the entire selected-prefix mean. It is not an average over only the original disjoint block means.')
    issue('ties-and-empty-minima',[4,5,6],'Argmin tie-breaking for L_hat, eta_hat and tau_hat is not stated. The optional fixed-J max-index selection is not a general tie convention. For finite data, eta_hat=m-1 is allowed by(10) but makes the sliding-window range in d_hat empty; no fallback is supplied. High-probability asymptotics do not by themselves define these bad finite-sample outputs.')
    issue('finite-sample-denominators',[3,4,5],'Population long-run variance is explicitly positive and finite. Generic consistent estimates can still be zero or negative on finite-sample events; estimator(8) is nonnegative but can be zero. The source does not fully specify square-root/sign/zero-division conventions. m>=2 is needed for the interior normal quantile and step-fit range, and follows eventually from the stated growth regime.')
    issue('dependence-parameters',[6,7,8],'Functional dependence replaces only innovation0 by an independent copy. Cumulative dependence sums over future indices, while long-run covariance sums over all integer lags. Condition3.1 retains both theta regimes and the exact gamma_theta radical/log threshold; gamma_theta is not the autocovariance gamma(k). The same theta must satisfy all moment, signal and block-rate conditions.')
    issue('rates-and-optional-defaults',[6,7,8,9],'Theorem3.2 has separate deterministic and probabilistic error terms. Theorem3.3 uses d_star with negative exponent theta/(theta-1). Rho=1/2, block length ceil(n^(1/3)) and geometric moment contraction are optional examples, not universal hypotheses. Early and late changes are allowed; tau need not be proportional ton.')
    issue('proof-and-application-scope',[7,8,9,16],'Brownian-bridge limits and KMT coupling interpret or prove the statistical results, not extra assumptions on observed noise. Oracle true-gap estimator(21) is not the actual estimator(12). Appendix proofs are excluded. The empirical interpretation of a search-index change as an epidemic starting date is application context and is not certified by this theorem census.')
    data=dict(paper_id=PID,unranked_auxiliary_passages=aux,statement_local_bindings=bindings,source_claim_references=refs,source_issues=issues,unresolved_external_prerequisites=[],ambient_prerequisites=['Real deterministic mean sequences and stationary centered processes; covariance and positive finite two-sided long-run variance.','Causal measurable processes driven by IID innovations, independent-copy coupling, Ltheta norms and summable functional-dependence tails.','Finite partial sums, integer floors and sliding windows, empirical prefix means, minimum/argmin operations and binary indicator step fitting.','Standard-normal quantiles for blockwise decisions; Brownian-bridge minimum distribution only as the global-test limiting interpretation.','Convergence in probability, little-o and stochastic O_P, deterministic versus random rate remainders and n-dependent change positions/gap sequences.','Tie, empty-window, exact block-boundary and finite-estimate division issues are recorded rather than filled with invented conventions. All statement definitions are available in main text; no appendix-only definition is needed.'],validation_limits='Main-text source fidelity and dependency scope only. No proof or library-availability verdict, and no certification of empirical causal interpretations. The recorded source indexing and finite-sample definition limitations remain unresolved.')
